The Google provider and Google Cloud IAM API normalize condition expressions by trimming surrounding whitespace and standardizing line breaks. However, heredocs (`<<EOT ... EOT`) can occasionally produce trivial plan diffs or whitespace drift depending on the exact provider version (`google` vs `google-beta`) and Terraform core version.

To eliminate any risk of whitespace drift in automated CI runners using `-detailed-exitcode`, formatting the CEL expressions as single-line strings with clean spacing is the industry best practice.

